  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Introduction</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Sleepwear Manufacturer for Comfort and Quality Brands</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>As a specialized sleepwear manufacturer based in Bangladesh, SDF Clothing understands that sleepwear requires exceptional comfort, skin-friendly materials, and durable construction for repeated washing. The sleepwear market encompasses diverse needs from basic pyjamas to luxurious robes, requiring expertise in soft fabrics and comfortable construction. Our facility delivers on these requirements with minimum orders of 300 pieces, making professional sleepwear manufacturing accessible to emerging brands and established labels expanding their loungewear collections.</p>
        
        <p>Bangladesh has established itself as a competitive sourcing destination for sleepwear and loungewear, combining cost advantages with developing expertise in soft fabric garments. Our sleepwear production leverages Bangladesh's textile ecosystem, offering international brands access to skilled labor, established supply chains for soft fabrics like modal and bamboo, and comprehensive manufacturing capabilities. The 300-piece minimum enables brands to test different sleepwear styles and fabric options without committing to large inventory positions, reducing risk while accessing factory-direct pricing.</p>
        
        <p>Our sleepwear manufacturing addresses the specific requirements of sleep garments: soft, skin-friendly fabrics that ensure comfort during extended wear, breathable materials that regulate temperature, durable construction that withstands frequent washing, and designs that balance comfort with aesthetic appeal. We work with modal, bamboo, cotton, satin, microfiber, and flannel to meet various comfort requirements and sustainability goals while maintaining OEKO-TEX certification for chemical safety.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Product Range</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">What We Manufacture</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Our sleepwear production encompasses multiple product categories designed for different preferences, climates, and market segments. Each category maintains our commitment to soft fabrics and comfortable construction while offering distinct comfort and style characteristics. We manufacture all categories from 300 pieces minimum, with the ability to mix categories within larger orders for comprehensive sleepwear collections.</p>
        
        <p>Pyjama sets represent our core sleepwear category, including coordinating tops and bottoms in various styles. We produce classic button-front pyjama tops with matching pants, t-shirt style pyjama tops with elastic-waist bottoms, short-sleeve pyjama sets for warm weather, and long-sleeve sets for cold weather. Pyjama sets use soft fabrics like modal, bamboo, or cotton in weights ranging from 140-180 GSM. The construction emphasizes flat seams and comfortable waistbands to prevent irritation during sleep. Pyjama sets are ideal for both men's and women's markets and represent versatile sleepwear staples.</p>
        
        <p>Nightgowns encompass various lengths and styles from short chemises to full-length gowns. We produce short nightgowns ending above the knee for warm weather or minimal coverage preferences, mid-length gowns ending mid-calf for balanced coverage, and full-length nightgowns for maximum coverage and warmth. Styles include simple A-line gowns, empire waist designs, and more elaborate styles with lace trim or decorative elements. Nightgowns use lightweight fabrics like modal, satin, or cotton voile in weights ranging from 130-160 GSM for drape and comfort. Nightgowns are primarily women's sleepwear and require careful attention to fit and modesty considerations.</p>
        
        <p>Robes include kimono-style robes with wide sleeves and wrap closures, bath robes for post-shower use, and lounging robes for relaxed home wear. We produce short robes ending at the knee for warm climates and mid-thigh, mid-length robes ending below the knee, and full-length robes for maximum warmth. Robes use fabrics including terry cloth for absorbency, modal for softness, and flannel for warmth. Construction features include tie closures, belt loops, and patch pockets. Robes require specialized construction for sleeves and closures, with minimums typically at 300 pieces per style. Robes bridge sleepwear and loungewear categories.</p>
        
        <p>Sleep shorts provide comfortable sleepwear for warm climates or customers who prefer minimal coverage. We produce elastic-waist sleep shorts in various inseam lengths from 3-inch to 9-inch depending on coverage preference. Sleep shorts use lightweight, breathable fabrics like cotton jersey, modal, or bamboo in weights ranging from 130-160 GSM. Construction emphasizes comfortable waistbands with soft elastic and flat seams to prevent irritation. Sleep shorts are popular in summer collections and warm climate markets. The simple construction makes sleep shorts cost-effective sleepwear options with quick production times.</p>
        
        <p>Camisoles and chemises offer lightweight sleepwear options particularly popular in women's markets. Camisoles are sleeveless tops with thin straps, while chemises are short dress-like sleepwear. We produce basic camisoles with simple construction, lace-trim camisoles for feminine appeal, and chemises with A-line or fitted silhouettes. These items use lightweight fabrics like modal, satin, or cotton voile in weights ranging from 120-150 GSM. The construction emphasizes comfortable straps and soft edges to prevent irritation. Camisoles and chemises are ideal for warm weather and can also serve as loungewear or layering pieces.</p>
        
        <p>Loungewear sets bridge sleepwear and casual wear, designed for comfort at home but suitable for relaxed public settings. We produce coordinated loungewear sets including tops and bottoms such as jogger-style pants with matching tops, hoodies with matching sweatpants, and casual dresses with coordinating cardigans. Loungewear uses comfortable fabrics like cotton fleece, French terry, or modal blends in weights ranging from 160-240 GSM depending on climate and intended use. Loungewear construction emphasizes comfort features like elastic waistbands and relaxed fits. Loungewear has expanded significantly as work-from-home trends have increased demand for comfortable home wear.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
        <table class="comparison">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Category</th>
              <th>Fabric GSM</th>
              <th>Key Features</th>
              <th>Best For</th>
              <th>Price Tier</th>
