  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__Label">Production Process</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Our Manufacturing Process</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Our sleepwear manufacturing follows a structured process designed to ensure consistent comfort, fabric quality, and construction durability. The process typically spans 60-75 days for first-time orders including sampling and production, with 45-60 days for repeat orders using approved fabrics and patterns. Sleepwear requires particular attention to fabric softness and seam construction to ensure comfort during sleep.</p>
        
        <p>The process begins with specification review, where we analyze your requirements including fabric preferences (modal, bamboo, cotton, satin), product category, size chart, and construction details. Our team provides feedback on technical feasibility and may suggest modifications to optimize manufacturability while maintaining design intent. This stage takes 2-3 days and ensures technical alignment before sampling begins. For sleepwear, we pay particular attention to fabric selection and seam placement to maximize comfort.</p>
        
        <p>Fabric sourcing and development follows specification review, taking 10-15 days for standard fabrics and 15-20 days for custom fabric development. Sleepwear fabrics undergo testing for softness, breathability, and skin safety before approval. We test fabrics for pilling resistance, color fastness, and shrinkage to ensure quality through repeated washing. If you require custom fabric development for specific colors, prints, or finishes, we coordinate with mills to produce sample yardage for testing and approval.</p>
        
        <p>Sample development for sleepwear takes 15-20 days for basic items and 20-25 days for complex garments like robes. Initial samples focus on construction and basic fit, with subsequent samples refining fit details, fabric hand feel, and finish quality. We provide detailed measurement reports comparing samples to your specifications and conduct wash testing to verify dimensional stability. Sleepwear samples require particular attention to seam comfort and fabric softness. You may request multiple sample rounds to perfect the design.</p>
        
        <p>Comfort testing is a critical step in sleepwear sampling that we conduct on all samples. We evaluate seam placement to ensure seams do not create pressure points during sleep, test elastic waistbands for comfortable tension without digging, and assess fabric hand feel for softness against skin. For robes, we test closure mechanisms to ensure they function smoothly without irritation. This comfort-focused testing ensures that the final product provides the comfort expected from quality sleepwear, reducing returns due to discomfort.</p>
        
        <p>Pattern grading for sleepwear requires careful attention to proportional scaling, particularly for items like robes and nightgowns where fit and coverage are important. The relationship between various measurements must be maintained through grading to ensure consistent fit across sizes. Our pattern makers use graded measurement systems that account for these relationships, producing size sets from XS to 4XL that maintain proportional fit. Grading takes 3-5 days for basic items and 5-7 days for complex garments with multiple components.</p>
        
        <p>Bulk production for sleepwear spans 30-40 days from fabric receipt for basic items like pyjama sets and sleep shorts. Robes and more complex items typically require 35-45 days. Cutting is performed with attention to grain direction for woven items to ensure consistent drape. Sewing lines are staffed by operators trained in soft garment construction, with particular expertise in flat seam techniques, elastic application, and delicate fabric handling. Quality checkpoints at each sewing operation verify seam integrity, stitch consistency, and construction accuracy.</p>
        
        <p>Final quality inspection uses AQL 2.5 standards for major defects and AQL 4.0 for minor defects, with additional testing for sleepwear-specific criteria. Inspection includes measurement verification against graded size charts, wash testing on random samples to verify dimensional stability, and construction quality verification. We also conduct visual inspection of stitching, finishing, and overall workmanship with particular attention to seam comfort. Detailed inspection reports with photos are provided before shipment.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Materials</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Fabric & Material Options</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Fabric selection is critical to sleepwear performance, affecting comfort, temperature regulation, durability, and care requirements. We offer multiple fabric options optimized for different climates, seasons, and comfort preferences. All fabrics are tested for skin safety and comfort before use in production.</p>
        
        <p>Modal is a semi-synthetic fiber produced from beech wood pulp, offering exceptional softness with excellent drape and color retention. Modal typically ranges from 130-160 GSM and resists pilling and fading better than cotton. The fabric has a smooth, silky hand feel that remains soft through repeated washing. Modal is breathable and moisture-wicking, making it comfortable for sleepwear. The beech wood used for modal is harvested from sustainably managed forests, making modal an eco-friendly option. Modal is ideal for premium sleepwear positioning and customers seeking luxurious comfort.</p>
        
        <p>Bamboo fabric offers sustainable softness with natural performance characteristics. Bamboo viscose is produced from bamboo grass, a rapidly renewable resource, and features a luxurious hand feel similar to silk. Bamboo fabrics typically range from 140-170 GSM and are naturally moisture-wicking and antimicrobial, reducing odor buildup during wear. The fabric has excellent drape and breathability, making it comfortable for sleepwear. Bamboo is more sustainable than conventional cotton, requiring less water and no pesticides. Bamboo fabrics cost approximately 10-15% more than cotton but appeal to eco-conscious customers.</p>
        
        <p>Cotton remains the traditional choice for sleepwear, providing natural comfort, breathability, and familiarity. Cotton sleepwear typically ranges from 150-200 GSM, with lighter weights for summer and heavier weights for winter. Cotton has natural temperature-regulating properties and absorbs moisture, making it comfortable for sleep. We offer combed cotton for enhanced softness and organic cotton certified by GOTS for sustainability. Cotton is ideal for classic sleepwear styling and customers prioritizing natural fibers. Cotton's familiarity and comfort make it a safe choice for broad market appeal.</p>
        
        <p>Satin fabric offers elegant sheen and smoothness for more luxurious sleepwear options. Satin is typically produced from polyester or silk blends in weights ranging from 130-160 GSM. The fabric has a smooth, glossy surface that feels cool against the skin and drapes beautifully. Satin sleepwear is particularly popular for nightgowns and robes where elegance and visual appeal are priorities. Polyester satin offers durability and easy care at competitive prices, while silk satin provides premium luxury at higher cost. Satin is ideal for premium positioning and special occasion sleepwear.</p>
        
        <p>Microfiber offers durability and easy care at competitive prices. Microfiber is a synthetic fabric typically ranging from 140-180 GSM that mimics the softness of natural fibers while offering superior durability and wrinkle resistance. The fabric resists pilling and fading, maintaining appearance through repeated washing. Microfiber is quick-drying and lightweight, making it suitable for travel sleepwear. However, microfiber does not provide the natural breathability of cotton or modal. Microfiber is ideal for value positioning and practical sleepwear where easy care is prioritized.</p>
        
        <p>Flannel provides warmth and comfort for cold weather sleepwear. Flannel is typically a cotton fabric brushed on one or both sides to create a soft, fuzzy surface. Flannel sleepwear ranges from 180-220 GSM, providing substantial warmth for cold climates. The brushed surface creates excellent insulation while maintaining breathability. Flannel is ideal for winter collections and markets with cold winters. The heavier weight and warmth come at slightly higher cost than lightweight sleepwear options. Flannel requires special care to maintain the brushed surface appearance.</p>
        
        <p>Organic cotton certified by GOTS (Global Organic Textile Standard) provides sustainable options for customers prioritizing organic materials. Organic cotton is grown without synthetic pesticides or fertilizers and processed without harmful chemicals. The fabric maintains the same comfort and performance as conventional cotton with the added benefit of environmental certification. Organic cotton typically costs 15-20% more than conventional cotton but enables sustainability claims that appeal to eco-conscious consumers. GOTS certification requires traceability throughout the supply chain.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
        <table class="comparison">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Fabric</th>
              <th>GSM Range</th>
              <th>Key Properties</th>
              <th>Best For</th>
              <th>Price Tier</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Modal</td>
              <td>130-160</td>
              <td>Soft, drape, pill-resistant</td>
              <td>Premium, luxurious comfort</td>
              <td>$$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Bamboo</td>
              <td>140-170</td>
              <td>Sustainable, antimicrobial, soft</td>
              <td>Eco-conscious, natural</td>
              <td>$$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Cotton</td>
              <td>150-200</td>
              <td>Natural, breathable, familiar</td>
              <td>Classic, versatile</td>
              <td>$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Satin</td>
              <td>130-160</td>
              <td>Elegant, smooth, sheen</td>
              <td>Premium, luxurious</td>
              <td>$$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Microfiber</td>
