  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Bangladesh Advantage</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Why Source Sleepwear from Bangladesh</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Bangladesh has established itself as a competitive sourcing destination for sleepwear and loungewear, combining cost advantages with developing expertise in soft fabric garments. The country's garment industry includes numerous factories focused on casual and sleepwear, with established supply chains for modal, bamboo, and other soft fabrics. This specialization, combined with competitive labor costs, makes Bangladesh an attractive option for sleepwear manufacturing.</p>
        
        <p>Labor costs in Bangladesh are significantly lower than in China, Vietnam, or Turkey, translating to 15-25% cost savings on finished sleepwear. However, the cost advantage does not come at the expense of quality. The Bangladeshi garment industry has developed particular expertise in soft garment production, with operators skilled in handling delicate fabrics like modal and satin, constructing comfortable seams, and maintaining consistent quality on lightweight materials. Our facility conducts regular training programs to ensure operators are proficient in the latest sleepwear construction techniques.</p>
        
        <p>Bangladesh's textile infrastructure includes knitting mills capable of producing modal, bamboo, and cotton blends suitable for sleepwear. The country has invested in knitting capacity for soft fabrics, reducing reliance on imported materials for basic sleepwear styles. This local sourcing reduces lead times and logistics costs compared to countries that rely entirely on imported fabrics. Our relationships with local knitting mills ensure priority allocation and consistent quality for sleepwear fabrics. For specialized fabrics or custom weights, we maintain relationships with international fabric suppliers.</p>
        
        <p>The country's export infrastructure includes experienced freight forwarders, customs brokers, and documentation specialists familiar with garment export requirements. Shipments from Bangladesh to major markets are routine, with multiple weekly sailings to Europe and North America. Ocean freight is particularly cost-effective for sleepwear given the lightweight nature of the garments, allowing efficient container utilization. The established export infrastructure reduces the risk of delays and documentation errors that can occur with less experienced sourcing locations.</p>
        
        <p>Workplace safety and social compliance across Bangladesh's garment industry have improved markedly since the comprehensive reforms that followed 2013. Our facility carries BSCI certification, covering fair wages, reasonable hours, and safe working conditions — standards that sleepwear buyers increasingly expect given how close-to-skin the product category is. Retailers who prioritize ethical sourcing treat this kind of certification as a baseline requirement now, and it meaningfully reduces the reputational risk that sourcing from Bangladesh once carried.</p>
        
        <p>Duty-free access to European markets through the Everything But Arms (EBA) arrangement provides Bangladesh garments with preferential tariff treatment, reducing import costs for EU customers. Similar preferential access exists for other markets including Canada, Australia, and Japan. This duty advantage can significantly impact landed costs for sleepwear, which are subject to standard garment duty rates in many markets. For brands targeting EU distribution, the duty savings can offset other costs and improve overall margins.</p>
        
        <p>The Bangladesh garment industry has developed specialized expertise in soft garment production, which directly translates to sleepwear manufacturing. Handling modal, bamboo, and other soft fabrics, constructing comfortable seams, and producing garments that maintain comfort through repeated washing are well-established skills in the country's workforce. This specialized expertise reduces the learning curve for new sleepwear styles and ensures consistent quality across production runs. The industry's experience with international casual wear brands also means that quality expectations for comfort and finish are well-understood.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">International Shipping</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Shipping to UK, USA, Australia & EU</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>We ship sleepwear to major international markets including the United Kingdom, United States, Australia, and European Union countries. Each market has specific requirements for documentation, duties, and shipping timelines that we navigate routinely. Our experience with international sleepwear shipments ensures your goods arrive on time and with proper documentation for customs clearance.</p>
        
        <p>Shipments to the United Kingdom typically take 30-35 days by ocean freight, including transit time and customs clearance. Air freight options reduce this to 7-10 days at significantly higher cost. The UK applies import duties on garments from Bangladesh, though rates vary by garment type and fabric composition. Sleepwear typically falls under specific HS codes for cotton or synthetic nightwear. We provide accurate classification and valuation to ensure proper duty calculation. Post-Brexit documentation requirements are handled to ensure smooth customs clearance.</p>
        
        <p>United States shipments take 25-30 days by ocean freight to West Coast ports and 35-40 days to East Coast ports. Air freight takes 5-7 days to major US airports. The US maintains normal trade relations with Bangladesh, with standard MFN duty rates applying to sleepwear. The US has specific labeling requirements for garments including fiber content in English and country of origin. We ensure all labels meet US Federal Trade Commission requirements. US customs may also inspect for compliance with textile fiber identification rules, which we address through proper documentation.</p>
        
        <p>Sleepwear orders bound for Australia move by ocean freight in 20-25 days to Sydney, Melbourne, or Brisbane, with a 7-10 day air freight option for urgent restocks. Because Bangladesh holds a free trade agreement with Australia, most garments clear duty-free once rules-of-origin requirements are met, and we structure production to satisfy those requirements from the outset. Australia's biosecurity checks are thorough, so we pay close attention to packaging and documentation to avoid hold-ups at the port.</p>
        
        <p>Sleepwear headed to the EU qualifies for duty-free entry under the Everything But Arms scheme for least-developed countries. Ocean freight takes 28-32 days to Northern European ports and 32-38 days further south, with a 5-8 day air freight option for tighter timelines. Documentation requirements include certificates of origin, itemized commercial invoices, and conformity declarations for certain fabrics, plus labeling that spells out fiber content and care instructions in the local language.</p>
        
        <p>Documentation for all markets includes commercial invoices, packing lists, bills of lading, certificates of origin, and any required certificates for regulated materials. For sleepwear, this may include certificates for fiber content if organic or sustainable materials are used. We provide all documentation in English and can arrange for translations if required by specific markets. Our documentation is prepared to meet both customs requirements and your internal accounting needs, with clear descriptions and accurate valuations.</p>
        
        <p>Incoterms can be structured according to your preferences, including FOB (Free On Board) Bangladesh for maximum control, CIF (Cost, Insurance, Freight) to destination port for convenience, or DDP (Delivered Duty Paid) for complete door-to-door service. For sleepwear, we typically recommend FOB for experienced importers, as the cost savings on ocean freight for lightweight garments make FOB economically advantageous. CIF and DDP options are available for brands seeking simplified logistics or those new to international sourcing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Certifications</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Quality Standards & Certifications</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Quality assurance and certification are fundamental to our sleepwear manufacturing process. Sleepwear requires particular attention to chemical safety and comfort due to prolonged skin contact during sleep. We maintain multiple certifications that verify our commitment to quality, sustainability, and social responsibility.</p>
        
        <p>OEKO-TEX Standard 100 certification applies to all our sleepwear fabrics, ensuring they are free from harmful substances including heavy metals, pesticides, and formaldehyde. This certification is particularly important for sleepwear that has prolonged skin contact during sleep. OEKO-TEX testing covers all fabric components including base materials, threads, trims, and elastic. We provide OEKO-TEX certificates for each material lot, enabling you to substantiate claims about chemical safety in your marketing materials. OEKO-TEX certification is essential for sleepwear marketed as skin-friendly or hypoallergenic.</p>
        
        <p>GOTS (Global Organic Textile Standard) certification applies to our organic cotton sleepwear, verifying organic fiber content and ensuring environmentally and socially responsible production throughout the supply chain. GOTS covers the entire process from organic farming to final garment labeling, ensuring that organic claims are substantiated. If you choose organic cotton for your sleepwear, GOTS certification provides credibility for organic marketing claims and is required by many retailers for organic textile products.</p>
        
        <p>Our BSCI (Business Social Compliance Initiative) certification is verified through independent third-party audits covering fair wages, reasonable working hours, prohibition of child labor, and safe working conditions across the full facility, not just the lines producing a given order. For sleepwear brands, that documentation gives you something concrete to point to when retailers or consumers ask how the product was actually made, and it's become a near-standard expectation rather than a differentiator.</p>
        
        <p>ISO 9001 certification applies to our quality management system, ensuring consistent processes for production and quality control. ISO 9001 requires documented procedures for all critical processes, regular internal audits, and continuous improvement. This certification provides assurance that our quality systems are systematic and repeatable, reducing variability between production runs. For sleepwear, this means consistent fabric quality, construction, and comfort across orders.</p>
        
        <p>WRAP (Worldwide Responsible Accredited Production) certification rounds out our compliance portfolio, focusing on workplace conditions and worker rights through an audit approach that differs from BSCI in methodology and emphasis. Sleepwear buyers selling through department stores or licensed brand programs often encounter retailer codes of conduct that specify WRAP by name, so holding it alongside our other certifications avoids delays when a buyer's compliance team asks for it specifically.</p>
        
        <p>Internal quality control processes supplement these certifications with day-to-day assurance specific to sleepwear production. We conduct in-line inspections during production, measuring garments at critical checkpoints to verify dimensional accuracy. Final inspection includes wash testing on random samples to verify dimensional stability and ensure garments maintain their fit after home laundering. We maintain records of all testing results, enabling traceability if issues arise after delivery. These internal processes ensure certifications translate to actual quality in finished sleepwear.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
